cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this paper or its companion artefacts, please cite it as below."
type: article
title: "Conformance, Cost, and Replication in Constrained LLM Coding Agents"
authors:
  - family-names: Rocchi
    given-names: Alessio
    affiliation: AIGEN Solutions
    email: rocchi.b.a@gmail.com
year: 2026
version: "1.4.3"
abstract: >
  Procedural protocols deliver +0.59 to +0.78 expected-utility gain over
  free prompting at log-token ratios 0.70–3.28 on 8 cells × 4 frontier
  models. However, 33–68% of procedurally-compliant runs still fail
  held-out semantic tests, exposing a conformance-without-semantics
  regime invisible to compliance-only metrics. We present a measurement
  framework that projects agent trajectories onto a behavior signature
  over conformance, target-correctness, robustness, and token cost,
  with a decisional cost-aware metric admitting a closed-form
  break-even threshold below which the protocol pays.
keywords:
  - LLM code generation
  - procedural constraints
  - stochastic dominance
  - asymmetric review
  - error decorrelation
  - predictability--cost trade-off
  - AST-level mutation testing
  - reviewer-family variation
